{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-167778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that \n\n$$\n\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nApplying this formula and the constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0aa3c2b2bcb3b53287e69e3e5d32ee83ff40f201c7d3f7b17f2b7db61575242"} {"question" "q-167778" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167778" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4\\cos(x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4\\cos(x)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n${g}^{″}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =8-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =8-2{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the second derivative, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-2{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0aa3c2b2bcb3b53287e69e3e5d32ee83ff40f201c7d3f7b17f2b7db61575242"} {"question" "q-167779" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167779" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following functions: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x},\\,g(x)=8x-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3},\\,h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4\\cos(x)$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\n${g}^{″}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4x$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nIf a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Slope $\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-167780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980664/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5004826172de3368d6f8834a4b58955139d2ad087249ca3682c2f70cc6ff855"} {"question" "q-